(1511303, 196351, 30049, '<td valign="top">Jason - I really enjoyed this image.  The first thing that hit me was the glow it seems to have.  Honestly, that was the reason I selected this as a favorite...I wanted to be able to find it after the challenge and see what you had done in post-processing to get that effect.<br/> <br/>The funny thing is - I didn''t notice the artifacts the first time around and I think that says something. Either I have a poor eye for the details and just missed it - or - (most likely) I got swept up in the image as art for what it is.  In retrospect I agree with some of the commenters in that the image would be better without the haloing artifacts, especially if you were to try and sell this as a print.<br/> <br/>As for differenct perspectives, angles, etc...you know what you had to work with and I think it is composed quite effectively.  Keep up the good work.  I look forward to seeing what else you come up with in the future.<br/> <br/>Barry</td>', 'Jason - I really enjoyed this image.  The first thing that hit me was the glow it seems to have.  Honestly, that was the reason I selected this as a favorite...I wanted to be able to find it after the challenge and see what you had done in post-processing to get that effect. The funny thing is - I didn''t notice the artifacts the first time around and I think that says something. Either I have a poor eye for the details and just missed it - or - (most likely) I got swept up in the image as art for what it is.  In retrospect I agree with some of the commenters in that the image would be better without the haloing artifacts, especially if you were to try and sell this as a print. As for differenct perspectives, angles, etc...you know what you had to work with and I think it is composed quite effectively.  Keep up the good work.  I look forward to seeing what else you come up with in the future. Barry', '2005-07-06 10:26:05.000000', NULL, 0),
