(1516212, 196834, 31399, '<td valign="top">kawhona you hit nail on the head...was drizzlin rain when I took the shot...dpc kings and queens coulda done wonders with this...but for mere mortal as I not too bad...better than my average...thanks all for the input and help as always, God''s blessings to you all.  Sonya</td>', 'kawhona you hit nail on the head...was drizzlin rain when I took the shot...dpc kings and queens coulda done wonders with this...but for mere mortal as I not too bad...better than my average...thanks all for the input and help as always, God''s blessings to you all.  Sonya', '2005-07-07 16:10:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1516397, 196143, 31534, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club!!! <br/> <br/>Composition: <br/>The composition of this shot is nice. I like that the subject "the moody fork" is not centered. <br/>Background/ Foreground <br/> <br/>I like the gray background on the left but the it appears a tad blown out on the right. Still over all does not distract from the fork.<br/>There does appear to be a smudge on the lower right. <br/> <br/>Camera Work: <br/> <br/>Focus is great. Lighting works. I would love to see some of the outtakes because I think other angles would be interesting.<br/>It is very hard to shoot metal with out getting glare and you only have a very small amount on the edge of the fork. <br/>I have invested in a soft box and that really makes a difference when shooting reflective ojects.<br/>You do amazing work with your Kodak camera. I can only imagine what you could do with a Nikon or a Cannon. (I have to be fair, even if I love my Nikon) <br/>Post-Processing: <br/> <br/>I can not comment on your post-processing because you did not include it in the comment field. Including this information helps us see what you have done, and can help teach other users how to use post processing to improve their pictures. <br/> <br/>My Opinion: <br/>I love shots that give some insight to the photographer and you have a wonderful sense of humor. You take pictures that please you and that is what will set you apart from other photographers. In looking at your other pictues I really like that your children are a part of your art, and seem to enjoy it with you. Even if you cover their face in sugar. =)<br/> <br/>You have a natural eye so keep shooting and sharing your work with us. <br/> <br/>I hope you find these comments to be helpful, thank you for allowing me to critique your picture. If you have any questions or concerns feel free to contact me via PM. <br/> <br/>Best of luck in your future photographic endeavors, <br/> <br/>Regards, <br/>Karen Doss <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club!!!  Composition: The composition of this shot is nice. I like that the subject "the moody fork" is not centered. Background/ Foreground  I like the gray background on the left but the it appears a tad blown out on the right. Still over all does not distract from the fork.There does appear to be a smudge on the lower right.  Camera Work:  Focus is great. Lighting works. I would love to see some of the outtakes because I think other angles would be interesting.It is very hard to shoot metal with out getting glare and you only have a very small amount on the edge of the fork. I have invested in a soft box and that really makes a difference when shooting reflective ojects.You do amazing work with your Kodak camera. I can only imagine what you could do with a Nikon or a Cannon. (I have to be fair, even if I love my Nikon) Post-Processing:  I can not comment on your post-processing because you did not include it in the comment field. Including this information helps us see what you have done, and can help teach other users how to use post processing to improve their pictures.  My Opinion: I love shots that give some insight to the photographer and you have a wonderful sense of humor. You take pictures that please you and that is what will set you apart from other photographers. In looking at your other pictues I really like that your children are a part of your art, and seem to enjoy it with you. Even if you cover their face in sugar. =) You have a natural eye so keep shooting and sharing your work with us.  I hope you find these comments to be helpful, thank you for allowing me to critique your picture. If you have any questions or concerns feel free to contact me via PM.  Best of luck in your future photographic endeavors,  Regards, Karen Doss ', '2005-07-07 17:30:18.000000', NULL, 0),
