(1516854, 196833, 23394, '<td valign="top">i had a similar entry a while back, and it was suggested to me that i could make the image more dynamic by rotating it to make the line more diagonal, from one corner to the other.  i did that, and i made a huge difference...something so simple.<br/> <br/>as far as setting up the shot, you might have chosen a more dynamic angle, rather than shooting it almost documentary-style from the side. look for ways to shoot your subject that bring your viewer into the image as a participant.<br/> <br/>good luck, have fun, and keep on shooting!</td>', 'i had a similar entry a while back, and it was suggested to me that i could make the image more dynamic by rotating it to make the line more diagonal, from one corner to the other.  i did that, and i made a huge difference...something so simple. as far as setting up the shot, you might have chosen a more dynamic angle, rather than shooting it almost documentary-style from the side. look for ways to shoot your subject that bring your viewer into the image as a participant. good luck, have fun, and keep on shooting!', '2005-07-07 21:17:22.000000', NULL, 0),
