(1853713, 197053, 28742, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GentleSoul:</b></div><hr/><i> Geez... I almost feel myself tearing up!  You really should add this to the Emotive gallery, too!<br/>Very nicely done. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>:) Thanks - done and done.</td>', 'Originally posted by GentleSoul: Geez... I almost feel myself tearing up!  You really should add this to the Emotive gallery, too!Very nicely done.  :) Thanks - done and done.', '2005-11-10 01:22:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1885057, 197237, 25232, '<td valign="top">I don''t understand the significance of the passport. It is clearly German, but was the man a war criminal, or a short order cook? Is he famous? Am I supposed to recognize this man? Why should I choose to or not to forgive this man? What has he done that he needs forgiveness?</td>', 'I don''t understand the significance of the passport. It is clearly German, but was the man a war criminal, or a short order cook? Is he famous? Am I supposed to recognize this man? Why should I choose to or not to forgive this man? What has he done that he needs forgiveness?', '2005-11-20 16:51:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1887137, 197237, 27845, '<td valign="top">This is a passport of a Frenchman issued under the Nazi regime. This means that he has either been forced to work for them, or has collaborated with them. The title of the picture was ill-chosen, it doesn''t reflect my thoughts on it very well, the word forgiven does not really fit to anyone involved.<br/>The fact that this passport lies in the museum suggests that it was not possible to return it to his relatives, or that there were none.<br/>And no, he is not famous.</td>', 'This is a passport of a Frenchman issued under the Nazi regime. This means that he has either been forced to work for them, or has collaborated with them. The title of the picture was ill-chosen, it doesn''t reflect my thoughts on it very well, the word forgiven does not really fit to anyone involved.The fact that this passport lies in the museum suggests that it was not possible to return it to his relatives, or that there were none.And no, he is not famous.', '2005-11-21 12:02:59.000000', NULL, 0),
